WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
Hi, in this video we will see how
computers talk. Before we do that, I would

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:10.290
like to give you an analogy of how
people talk. In this room we have John,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:15.330
Bob, and Mary, and when John wants to
talk to Mary he says, "Hi, Mary! This is John.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.690
How are you doing?" Now, when they're in the same room

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:23.550
they're sharing the same medium, which is the air and all of them, Bob and Mary

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:29.310
hear (listen) to this message but only Mary
responds because it's addressed to

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:34.890
Mary. In the same way, when computers
want to talk they share a medium. In this

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:40.649
example all these three computers are
sharing a cable. This is how networks

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:45.930
were built in the past so you have NIC
cards for each of these computers and

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:51.210
they have their own MAC addresses. Now,
let's say if A wants to talk to B, what

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.680
A does is it sends a message to B
which looks similar to this:

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:05.100
"Hey B, you know you use the MAC address to address B, this is A talking and here

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.000
is my message:

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.400
"How are you doing?" Now, when this message
is put on this medium everybody on this

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.310
medium can listen to it. So in this case
B and C can listen to this message.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.000
Now what happens is, when C looks at
this message it sees that it's

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.920
addressed to B so just silently ignores
it and B, when it gets this message,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.750
it sees that 'Oh! This message is
addressed to me, so let me reply" and when

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:37.140
it decides to reply what B does is: "I
want to know who is talking" so, it looks

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.030
like the original message and sees it's
A who is talking, so it says "Hey,

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.500
A, this is B" and the actual message "I'm
doing good"

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.750
that's how computer talk.

